1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,470
Five questions from the Web Reality Checks fixtures.

2
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:09,300
Every answer comes from a test or an evidence file.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:18,020
Q1 · Episode 26: flawed list of 100 articles.

4
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:25,780
How many SELECT statements does the counter report?

5
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:37,470
B. 101: one list query plus 100 author lookups.

6
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:44,420
The JOIN reports 1. A hidden extra query shows as 102.

7
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:56,200
Q2 · Episode 15: same key, quantity 1 changed to 3.

8
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:02,630
What does the corrected endpoint return?

9
00:01:08,630 --> 00:01:14,440
C. 422: same key, different request.

10
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:20,250
The order count stays at 1.

11
00:01:20,250 --> 00:01:31,180
Q3 · Episode 23: a save hits a locked database.

12
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:36,650
What does the fixture return?

13
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:47,390
B. 503: database busy, retryable.

14
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:54,970
409 is only for a failed version check.

15
00:01:54,970 --> 00:02:04,680
Q4 · Episode 1: Alice asks for Bob's project,

16
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:11,150
with spoofed user-id claims. What status?

17
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:22,950
C. 404: the server never reads the claims.

18
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:28,750
The control proves the old endpoint returned 200.

19
00:02:28,750 --> 00:02:38,510
Q5 · Episode 17: polling every 5 s instead of 30 s.

20
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:45,010
At 570 s, how old is the measurement?

21
00:02:51,010 --> 00:02:58,690
C. 570 s: 119 polls instead of 19, one collector sample.

22
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:02,880
Fetching faster does not observe faster.

23
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:10,140
Score yourself. Every answer is in an evidence file.

24
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:13,370
The repository, linked below.
